1. no login at all
  connect: ok
  send: ok=0 code=530
    S: 530 5.7.0 Authentication required
2. CRAM-MD5: the client proves it knows the password, it never sends it
  connect: ok
  [server] message stored, logged in as: ann
  send: ok=1 code=250
    C: AUTH CRAM-MD5
    C: ****
    S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
3. a wrong password
  connect: authentication failed
    C: AUTH CRAM-MD5
    C: ****
    S: 535 5.7.8 Authentication credentials invalid
4. PLAIN without TLS: the client refuses
  connect: no TLS: the password is not sent in the clear (allowPlainAuth)
5. PLAIN with allowPlainAuth (the transcript hides the password)
  connect: ok
  [server] message stored, logged in as: ann
  send: ok=1 code=250
    C: AUTH PLAIN ****
    S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
6. a URL with a password: the server does not offer STARTTLS (and it is required)
